 # Burrows-Wheeler Transform
 ## Overview
-The Burrows-Wheeler Transform (BWT) is a reversible permutation scheme that re-sorts a block of data according to its local context, organizing it into a form that is highly compressible for subsequent entropy coding [S1, S2]. It is distinguished from linear decorrelation transforms by rearranging symbol positions rather than changing values [S1, S2]. Komma et al. [KFDB07] compared its compressibility against other transforms for volume data compression [S1, S2].
